<title>UK: KfW unit sets $250 million four-year Eurobond.</title>
<headline>KfW unit sets $250 million four-year Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Nikko Europe.</p>
<p> BORROWER   KFW INTERNATIONAL FINANCE</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  KREDITANSTALT FUER WIEDERAUFBAU</p>
<p> AMT	  $250 MLN  COUPON     6.375     MATURITY    09.JUL.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.15    PAY DATE    09.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.625     REOFFER    99.75     SPREAD	+7 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/GB/DE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  GERMANY   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.225     SELL CONC  1.40	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.375 PCT U.S. T-NOTE DUE 15.MAY.00 -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
